(799078, 86230, 4493, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments and the ribbon. My daughter and I were in vacation in Tennessee and had driven up to Cades Cove as it approached sunset. The mist/fog was beginning to set in. This shot was taken as we approached the park. I pulled over and walked back to this location and fired of about 6 shots. I used my Sigma 12-24mm lens @ 12mm for this shot. I spot metered near the light on the pavement in the left of the frame. Metering on the light itself or the beams caused the shutter to be to fast making the beams nearly invisible and the gravel almost black. We had a great trip and I have some other wonderful foggy shots from that drive we took with the windows down!<br/> <br/>-danny</td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments and the ribbon. My daughter and I were in vacation in Tennessee and had driven up to Cades Cove as it approached sunset. The mist/fog was beginning to set in. This shot was taken as we approached the park. I pulled over and walked back to this location and fired of about 6 shots. I used my Sigma 12-24mm lens @ 12mm for this shot. I spot metered near the light on the pavement in the left of the frame. Metering on the light itself or the beams caused the shutter to be to fast making the beams nearly invisible and the gravel almost black. We had a great trip and I have some other wonderful foggy shots from that drive we took with the windows down! -danny', '2004-07-07 01:53:14.000000', NULL, 0),
